    2. resource_efficiency (maximize, no upper bound)
       Q: There is no ceiling on resource efficiency, so the optimiser may legitimately run all machines at maximum speed and schedule zero idle time to push the KPI higher — potentially raising energy draw by 30–40% and sustaining operator fatigue near the 0.4 limit for the entire shift. Should an absolute throughput or energy cap apply (e.g. no more than 120% of the shift baseline consumption), or is unconstrained maximisation acceptable so long as the fatigue and noise hard constraints hold?
